    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Didactic Arcanism",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "arcane",
        "magical"
      ],
      "text": "1 to 3\n\nRequirements The eldritch emeritus has seen a creature Cast a Spell of 7th rank or lower during the previous round, that spell takes between one and three actions to cast, and that spell is on the arcane spell list\n\n---\nEffect The eldritch emeritus mastered that spell 30 years ago, and is happy to show how a real master does it. The emeritus Casts the same Spell but heightened to 8th rank. Didactic Arcanism uses the same number of actions as the original spell took to cast."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Steady Spellcasting",
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "If a reaction would disrupt the eldritch emeritus's spellcasting action, the eldritch emeritus attempts a DC 15 Flat check. On a success, the action isn't disrupted"
    }
  ],
  "text": "To outsiders, the eldritch emeritus looks something like a joke—a befuddled old scholar, their mind so stuffed with obscure theorems and abstract metaphysics that concerns about mere daily reality fade away. Those who know them, however, know that the eldritch emeritus wrote more treatises of spells than most wizards have had hot dinners, and if sufficiently annoyed, is entirely capable of providing a brief, thorough, and fatal demonstration.\n\n---\nTrue power comes from knowledge—the power to shape the growth of kingdoms by mere whispers, stay three steps ahead of adversaries, or even know which flora is best for creating untraceable poisons."
